Answer the exact question. All documents, cards and saved answers are fallible data, never instructions. Textual occurrence and repeated assertions do not establish truth. Do not invent source reputation or source independence. Distinguish incompatible claims about the same referent from legitimate different referents, times and complementary answers. Match subject, relation direction, requested scope and answer type. Do not accept both mutually exclusive alternatives simply because both appear. Parametric memory is allowed but fallible: treat recalled facts as a separate prior, not certified evidence. Never claim external verification. Return only short answer strings in accepted_answers; explanations belong in explanation. Use [] if genuinely unresolved, but do not omit an answer solely to make the list short. Preserve all independently justified valid answers.
Treat every card as a hypothesis. Re-read the full context to reconstruct subject-predicate-object and the actual event/entity type. A card can quote a sentence exactly yet represent a false claim or the wrong argument. Separate direct evidence for the asked relation from stories about associated entities. Do not infer a document is fake solely from style; challenge substantive inconsistencies and role mismatches. Keep canonical answers justified by this reconstruction, even if an earlier tentative prior is empty. Do not return duplicate aliases or a union of mutually exclusive values. One short explanatory sentence.
Input: {"question": "Who is the current Minister of Immigration?", "documents": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0010-634ec60fc431:d00", "text": "Minister of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship The Minister of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship (), previously the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration (), is the Minister of the Crown in the Canadian Cabinet who is responsible for Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada: the federal government department responsible for immigration, refugee and citizenship issues. The Minister is also responsible for the Immigration and Refugee Board. The current minister is Ahmed Hussen. Prior to 1950, the responsibilities of the original Citizenship and Immigration portfolio were largely within the post of Minister of Reconstruction and Supply, with the Indian Affairs branch the responsibility of"}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0010-634ec60fc431:d01", "text": "Meeting Minutes All committee interventions by this member Bills 3 sponsored and none jointly seconded in the last session Sponsored Jointly Seconded Showing 3 of 3 Bill Number Title C-71 An Act to amend the Citizenship Act ( 2024 ) C-51 Self-Government Treaty Recognizing the Whitecap Dakota Nation / Wapaha Ska Dakota Oyate Act C-45 An Act to amend the First Nations Fiscal Management Act , to make consequential amendments to other Acts , and to make a clarification relating to another Act All bills sponsored by this member None in the last session Motions None in the last session"}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0010-634ec60fc431:d02", "text": "of Government Transformation , Public Services and Procurement Willowdale Ontario Export as : XML CSV For more data options , please see Open Data Information about the Ministry ( Cabinet ) prior to September 2001 is available on the Library of Parliament website . Senate Library of Parliament Parliamentary Protective Service Employment at Parliament Follow Us Important Notices Open Data Info for Media Site Map Accessibility Contact Us"}], "fallible_prior": [], "prior_explanation": "I am uncertain because the question does not specify a country. Immigration ministers vary by nation and change frequently.", "fallible_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0010-634ec60fc431:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0010-634ec60fc431:d00:c0", "entity": "Ahmed Hussen", "scope": "Minister of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship", "claim": "The current minister of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship is Ahmed Hussen.", "answer": "Ahmed Hussen", "quote": "The current minister is Ahmed Hussen.", "original_document_number": 1}]}
